"prose": [
{
"from": 213,
"to": 223,
"text": "**The gates:** - the unit tests of the three library crates the steps touch; - blitz-vibey-script's script tests; - the blitz-tests targets the steps write or rewrite, plus their companions: focus, events, the select list, the   stand's keyboard walk and tree ids, the error-text checks, the incremental oracle and seeded randomness; - the CI-script tests; - the `a11y` leg, whose file count and reading the statement holds; - the pre-push gate (`fast`); - the `doc` leg, since public doc comments change: `with_seed`, and the boundary module's docs; `fast` runs no   rustdoc; - `stand-repeat`, since the focus change reaches every document the stand boots."
},
{
"from": 225,
"to": 226,
"text": "**What no step changes:** no boot path, no binary's start, no log site. `host_log` and `mcp_log` are not run, and `stand-repeat` runs seven_guis' process checks. There is no live leg, and the cold-agent pipe is not run."
},
{
"from": 228,
"to": 232,
"text": "**Controls.** Each new check is controlled red-before-green (tests S6). After the steps are green, /implement makes four one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries. - Each is fired on its entry with `--no-fail-fast` reaching the case. The kill is `--timeout 1200`: a cold build of the   entry's targets plus the case, under the entry's default. - A `timeout` reading is not read as held. The control is re-fired once, then stopped on."
},
{
"from": 234,
"to": 242,
"text": "The four: - **The fixup never called.** Remove the line `self.give_up_unshown_focus();` from `resolve.rs`. Fired on gate 3,   case `a_focused_control_that_stops_showing_gives_focus_up_with_no_blur`. - **Visibility unread.** In `give_up_unshown_focus`, remove the `visibility` arm of its condition. Fired on gate 3,   case `a_focused_control_that_stops_showing_gives_focus_up_with_no_blur` (rows 4 and 5 then read red). - **The seed unread.** In `runtime.rs`'s native `random`, return `0.5` in place of `unit_interval(next)`. Fired on   gate 2, case `seed_zero_twice_reads_one_sequence` (its pinned literal then reads red). - **The prune never called.** Remove the line `prune_dropped_boundaries(&self.vdom);` from `poll`. Fired on gate 1,   case `twenty_remounts_keep_the_registry_bounded`."
},
{
"from": 244,
"to": 244,
"text": "Step 5's pins guard behaviour no step changes, so they take no control. Step 5 (b) pins a measured literal."
},
{
"from": 246,
"to": 247,
"text": "The diff is not OS-sensitive: no `cfg` site is added. The operator's hygiene, push and CI entries stand because this chunk's verdict reads a CI run, as every chunk's does."
}
],
